	"rows": [
		{
			"id": "ex8wWZ8KfqZiMJuTb",
			"description": "Laspistol, Common Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The commonest sidearm in the Imperium: issued to Guard officers, Munitorum staff, hive militia and anyone who rates a weapon above a stub pistol. Depicted constantly across Black Library Guard fiction (Gaunt's Ghosts, the Ciaphas Cain novels) as the backup weapon of choice once a soldier's lasgun runs dry or their hands are full.\n\nDesign: Damage is the fixed laspistol anchor (4d(2) burn). Average roll 14 already kills an unarmoured man (HP 10) in 1-2 hits per framework.md; the (2) divisor is carried by every las weapon in the las lineup so a laspistol still means something against flak (DR 30, effective 15): 4d(2) penetrates 33.6% of hits there, but never against carapace (DR 70, effective 35) — 0% of hits get through. Acc 3 is the top of the framework's pistol band (1-3): a beam has no drop and no recoil, so it sits above the slug-throwing pistols. Range, RoF and shot count are not anchored, so they're built from scratch for a hand-held energy pistol: a smaller accumulator than a lasgun's gives roughly half the lasgun's shot count (30 vs. 60), and the short emitter keeps Bulk and ST modest. RoF 3 represents the selector's rapid-pulse setting rather than a sustained full-auto mode. Handling: min ST 5 matches framework.md's √(10×weight) formula almost exactly for a 2.5 lb pistol (√25=5), so it needs no adjustment - a low-recoil beam sidearm this light sits right at the formula's baseline. Bulk -2 and Rcl 1 are ordinary low-recoil pistol figures.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "3",
			"base_value": "150",
