		{
			"id": "ezNye66gtm2BUWAXt",
			"description": "Laspistol, Compact \"Hostile Environment\" Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A shortened laspistol favoured by commissars and naval officers who need a weapon that won't print under a greatcoat; several Commissar characters across Guard fiction are shown carrying a compact sidearm distinct from a trooper's full-size laspistol, though no single novel gives it a formal designation, so \"Hostile Environment Pattern\" here is a descriptive label rather than an attested in-universe name.\n\nDesign: Damage stays at the fixed laspistol anchor (4d(2) burn) — shrinking the emitter doesn't change the lasing chemistry or the focusing coil that gives it the (2) divisor, only its housing. A smaller cell drops the shot count to 20 and shortens effective range; the shorter barrel worsens Acc by 1 (2 against the full-size pistol's 3) but improves Bulk to -1, which is the standard GURPS trade a concealable pistol makes against a full-size one. Handling: min ST corrected to 4 (√(10×2)≈4.5, rounded down) from a previous flat 5 copied from the full-size pistol above - a lighter, shorter housing needs a hair less strength to control even though the lasing chemistry is unchanged. Bulk -1 and Rcl 1 are unchanged.",
