		{
			"id": "e38ToVKwUIras-fWj",
			"description": "Lasgun, Kantrael Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The most widely issued lasgun in the Astra Militarum, standard Departmento Munitorum pattern and the rifle carried by the Cadian shock troops in codex background and countless Black Library novels.    design: >- Damage is the fixed lasgun anchor, 7d(2) burn. Beams have no drop, so the lasgun's 400/1200 range is as long as the hellgun's and the long-las's is twice that; the autogun's longer max range (2000) is ballistic carry. Range/RoF/shots are not anchored and are built to match the lasgun's lore signature: a 60-shot accumulator that recharges off almost any power source, and a fire selector giving single, burst and full-auto settings (abstracted here as RoF 10 for full-auto; treat single fire as RoF 1 at the GM's discretion). Required lasgun-vs-armour check (framework.md, exact dice distribution): 7d(2) averages 24.5 and penetrates flak (DR 30, effective 15) on 97.8% of hits, matching \"punches flak\"; against carapace (DR 70, effective 35) it penetrates 0.6% of hits, matching \"almost never carapace\" (the user's own figure, kept as given). Against Astartes power armour (DR 100, effective 50) it penetrates 0% of hits, matching \"useless against power armour.\" The Hot-shot pack usage reuses the hellgun anchor (8d(3) burn) exactly, since a hot-shot pack is explicitly the same overcharge trick as a hellgun's power cell, just dropped into an ordinary lasgun for one shot. The Overcharge usage is a milder, non-hellgun field expedient stepped up from the lasgun anchor: +1 die (8d burn, average 28), no armour divisor, limited shots — it still clears flak (30.5% of hits) but fails against mesh (3.9%) and carapace (0% of hits), because the whole point of the divisor is what an overcharge pack doesn't add. Handling: min ST corrected to 9 for all three usages (standard, hot-shot pack, overcharge shot - it's the same physical rifle, so they share one ST figure), matching framework.md's own worked example of √(10×8)≈9 for an 8 lb rifle almost exactly. The previous ST 6 on this and every other lasgun pattern in this file understated the handling of a shoulder rifle by three whole points against the framework's explicit guidance - it has been corrected here and on every pattern below. RoF 10 (full-auto) and RoF 1 (single fire, hot- shot and overcharge, since neither the hot-shot pack nor the overcharge cell is rated for autofire) reflect the lasgun's actual fire-selector modes rather than a single blanket value; Bulk -4. Rcl 1 (user direction): a laser has no kick. It was Rcl 2 while bursts were one roll with a hit per point of margin; with automatic fire now rolled per round at a further -Recoil each (the simulator's house rule), Rcl 1 already puts the tenth round of a burst at -9 as the rifle wanders.",
