		{
			"id": "eaOJ59D6DW0z5QrS3",
			"description": "Lasgun, Mars Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Forge-produced to exacting Mechanicus ritual-specification, the Mars pattern is prized for durability and is common among Skitarii auxilia and Mechanicus-aligned regiments; codex and Forge World background repeatedly single it out as the most rugged of the mass-production lasgun patterns.\n\nDesign: Same fixed lasgun anchor (7d(2) burn) as every pattern in this family — the difference is build quality, not lasing power. Extra shielding and a reinforced housing add roughly 1.5 lb and 1 ST over the Kantrael baseline and justify the higher cost. GCS has no reliability/ malfunction stat, so the pattern's noted ruggedness is left as lore flavour rather than a mechanical bonus. Handling: min ST corrected to 10 (√(10×9.5)≈9.7, rounded up), one point over the corrected Kantrael figure of 9, matching the extra shielding and reinforced housing this pattern is built with. RoF, Bulk and Rcl are unchanged from the Kantrael baseline.",
