		{
			"id": "e2vjiQO48qYwZwhzd",
			"description": "Lasgun, Lucius Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A lighter, sleeker lasgun pattern; Gaunt's Ghosts establishes the Tanith First's lasguns as this pattern, and the novels note it as reliable but less tolerant of mud and rough handling than the heavier Munitorum-standard patterns.\n\nDesign: Damage fixed at the lasgun anchor (7d(2) burn) — a slimmer frame doesn't change the lasing chamber's output. The lighter build lowers ST requirement and improves Bulk to -3 (vs. -4 for the Kantrael/Mars/ Accatran patterns), reflecting the more compact, less rugged design. Its documented fragility in mud has no GCS reliability stat to hang on, so it's recorded here as flavour only. Handling: min ST corrected to 8 (√(10×6.5)≈8.1), a point below the corrected Kantrael figure of 9, for the lighter, slimmer frame Gaunt's Ghosts describes - still following the framework's sqrt formula, just from a lower starting weight. RoF and Rcl are unchanged; Bulk stays one step better than the standard pattern's -4.",
