		{
			"id": "ec-QLUJ0NyxxDyD-8",
			"description": "Lasgun, Triplex Pattern",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Named for its three-position fire selector, the Triplex pattern adds a mechanical 3-round burst mode on top of the usual single/full-auto options found across the standard lasgun family.\n\nDesign: Damage fixed at the lasgun anchor (7d(2) burn) for both modes — the selector changes how the shots are grouped, not the lasing output. The controlled 3-round burst gets a +1 Acc bump over the full-auto line (7 vs. 6) to represent the tighter grouping a mechanical burst limiter gives compared to unrestrained full-auto fire. Handling: min ST corrected to 9 for both modes (√(10×8.5)≈9.2, same weight class as the Accatran pattern), sharing one figure since it's the same physical rifle on two fire-selector settings. RoF 3 for the controlled burst and RoF 10 for full-auto correctly reflect two different mechanical modes rather than one blanket rate copied across both lines. Bulk -4; Rcl 1 on both automatic modes, as the Kantrael.",
