		{
			"id": "eXXfECcrkeRwbzurU",
			"description": "Lascarbine",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A cut-down lasgun issued to vehicle crew, tank riders and scouts who need something more compact than a full-length rifle; short-barrelled lasguns of this kind appear throughout Guard fiction as tank-crew and support-trooper sidearms.\n\nDesign: Damage fixed at the lasgun anchor (7d(2) burn); the lasing chemistry that produces that figure doesn't depend on barrel length the way a slugthrower's velocity does, so the carbine's shorter emitter only costs Acc and effective range (5/270-810 vs. the full lasgun's 6/400-1200) while buying a much better Bulk (-2) for cramped vehicle interiors. Handling: min ST corrected to 8 (√(10×6)≈7.75), following the same formula as every other lasgun pattern in this file rather than the previous flat 5 shared with the pistols. RoF 10 and Rcl 1 are unchanged.",
			"tags": [
