		{
			"id": "eFnP3xPjtRy2_ffwz",
			"description": "Hellpistol",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A compact hot-shot sidearm issued alongside the hellgun to Militarum Tempestus officers and Inquisitorial agents who need a backup weapon that can still trouble carapace armour.\n\nDesign: Scaled from the hellgun anchor (8d(3) burn) by -2d, armour divisor unchanged: the laspistol is three dice below the lasgun (4d vs 7d, ratio 0.57), plasma pistol 0.67 and bolt pistol 0.83 of their rifles, so a hellpistol at 6d (0.75) sits mid-band. Stepping down only one die (7d(3)) would give it lasgun-average damage with a hellgun divisor, a mini-hellgun. The (3) divisor is what lets it trouble carapace at all, so it carries over. Average roll 21 against carapace (DR 70, effective 23.3) penetrates 27.9% of hits (Sororitas 3.6%, Mk VII 0.1%, flak 99.5%): a real threat to carapace, far less reliable than the full-size hellgun's 82.1%. Range matches the laspistol (beams do not drop) and Acc 3 the laspistol's. Shot count is lower than an ordinary laspistol's because a hot-shot cell packs more energy per shot into the same volume, so it burns out faster. Handling: min ST 6 (√(10×3)≈5.5, rounded up for the reinforced housing a hot-shot cell needs even at pistol scale) sits a point above an ordinary laspistol's ST 5 for the same reason the full hellgun needs more ST than a standard lasgun. RoF 3, Bulk -2 and Rcl 1 are ordinary pistol figures.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Militarum Tempestus"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "2",
			"base_value": "700",
			"base_weight": "3 lb",
			"weapons": [
