		{
			"id": "eRtelhWXkujAhZk6c",
			"description": "Hellgun",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The signature weapon of the Militarum Tempestus Scions, an overcharged lasgun-pattern rifle purpose-built to beat armour a standard lasgun can't; its role as the carapace-killer of Imperial small arms is consistent background across Scion-focused fiction and codex material.\n\nDesign: Damage is the fixed hellgun anchor, 8d(3) burn. Sanity check against the framework's stated purpose, computed by exact dice distribution: average roll 28, armour divisor 3 cuts carapace's DR 70 to an effective 23.3, so 8d(3) penetrates carapace on 82.1% of hits — it reliably beats carapace, confirming \"built to beat carapace\" with no adjustment needed. Against Sororitas power armour (DR 85, effective 28.3) it still gets through 46.0% of the time; against Astartes power armour (DR 100, effective 33.3) that drops to 13.0%, matching hellgun's place below the boltgun as an infantry-scale weapon. Shot count (40) is lower than a standard lasgun's 60 to reflect the hungrier, hotter cell. Handling: min ST corrected to 9 (√(10×9)≈9.5, rounded down), matching the framework formula for a 9 lb rifle - a point above a standard lasgun's corrected ST of 9 at the same nominal weight would suggest, reflecting the extra containment shielding an overcharged cell needs; the previous flat ST 7 undersold how much of a handful a hellgun actually is. RoF 10, Bulk -4 and Rcl 1 are unchanged.",
			"tags": [
				"Missile Weapon",
				"Imperium",
				"Militarum Tempestus"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "2",
			"base_value": "1600",
			"base_weight": "9 lb",
			"weapons": [
