		{
			"id": "e9SZZAY1iFRye2LJj",
			"description": "Charge Pack, Laspistol",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The standard rechargeable accumulator cell for a laspistol; widely depicted as rechargeable from almost any generator, or slowly by a hand-crank in the field when nothing else is available.\n\nDesign: Pure ammunition item, no weapon stats of its own — it's what \"30(3)\" on the laspistol's shot line refers to. Capacity matches the common pattern laspistol's shot count.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "3",
			"base_value": "10",
			"base_weight": "0.5 lb",
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "esMJXDeUvRjbcL6Kx",
			"description": "Charge Pack, Lasgun",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The standard 60-shot accumulator cell shared by every lasgun pattern in Munitorum service; its 60-round capacity is one of the most consistently repeated facts about the lasgun across Imperial Guard background material.\n\nDesign: Pure ammunition item matching the \"60(3)\" shot line common to every lasgun pattern above.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "3",
			"base_value": "15",
			"base_weight": "1 lb",
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "e8UIaYOuyFSbYfSsl",
			"description": "Charge Pack, Long-Las",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A higher-capacity, tighter-tolerance cell built for the long-las's focusing chamber; sniper teams are consistently shown carrying extra packs rather than relying on field recharge, since a spoiled cell ruins the rifle's accuracy.\n\nDesign: Pure ammunition item matching the long-las's \"20(3)\" shot line. Restricted to LC 2 in line with the rifle's own sniper-issue legality.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "2",
			"base_value": "40",
			"base_weight": "1.5 lb",
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "ewKSNyoSP3aeDMBWm",
			"description": "Hot-Shot Power Pack",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The superheated power cell standard to the hellgun and hellpistol, and the same item Guardsmen famously slot into an ordinary lasgun to turn it into a one-shot hellgun in a pinch — a trick referenced repeatedly in Guard-focused fiction and RPG background alike.\n\nDesign: Pure ammunition item; it's what unlocks the \"Hot-shot pack\" usage line on the Kantrael lasgun above (and, at the GM's discretion, on any other lasgun pattern) as well as powering the hellgun/hellpistol's standard fire. The overheat risk after use is a roleplaying consequence noted on those weapons' usage lines rather than a GCS stat, since the schema has no malfunction field (the plasma gun anchor has the same limitation).",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Militarum Tempestus"
			],
			"tech_level": "11",
			"legality_class": "2",
			"base_value": "60",
			"base_weight": "1 lb",
			"quantity": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "ewZMWr3JzwpZ-IdOL",
			"description": "Overcharge Power Pack",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A lasgun accumulator cell deliberately overloaded for extra punch per shot — a field-expedient trick short of a true hot-shot conversion, well short of hellgun performance but easier to come by.\n\nDesign: Pure ammunition item backing the \"Overcharge shot\" usage line on the Kantrael lasgun above: +1 die of damage, no armour divisor, and a short 10-shot life before the cell is spent.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Astra Militarum"
			],
			"tech_level": "10",
			"legality_class": "3",
			"base_value": "40",
			"base_weight": "1 lb",
			"quantity": 1
		}
	]
